# TLS server, CHUNKING reception with TLS shutdown mid-chunk
gnutls
#
# A TLS session that goes away while a BDAT chunk is still being read leaves the
# server holding readers, and a transfer buffer, belonging to a session that has
# ceased to exist.  Reading has to stop there.  Going on would either reach into
# the released buffer or take the rest of the chunk from the socket in clear, on
# the connection the peer negotiated encryption for.
#
# Chunk arithmetic - 88 declared, 20 sent, so 68 bytes are still outstanding when
# the session goes.  The ">>> " prefix suppresses the trailing CRLF the client
# would otherwise add, so the payload is exactly the 20 characters after it and
# the header line it starts is left unfinished.  Both halves of that shape are
# load-bearing.  The chunk has to be short, so that the session goes away with
# the transfer still owed data: a reader which treated what arrived as the whole
# of the message would accept a message the peer never finished sending.  And the
# line has to be unfinished, so that the shutdown is what the reader meets next -
# a line completed with a bare linefeed would instead be rejected for not being
# CRLF terminated, which is a check made as each header line is taken.
#
# The reply is matched in full rather than as just "421" because the receive
# timeout answers with a 421 of its own, and a loose match would be satisfied by
# the very behaviour this test exists to reject - a server that keeps reading the
# plain socket has nothing to read there, and says so when the timeout expires.
#
# Nothing is offered in clear after the shutdown, so the server has nothing
# unconsumed to reset over and its close is clean.  That is what lets the end of
# file be asserted here, and asserting it is half the point: a server which
# answered 421 and then left the socket usable would pass on the reply alone.
#
exim -DSERVER=server -DSRV=tls -bd -oX PORT_D
****
#
client-anytls 127.0.0.1 PORT_D
??? 220
EHLO rhu.barb
??? 250-
??? 250-SIZE
??? 250-8BITMIME
??? 250-PIPELINING
??? 250-CHUNKING
??? 250-STARTTLS
??? 250 HELP
STARTTLS
??? 220
EHLO rhu.barb
??? 250-
??? 250-SIZE
??? 250-8BITMIME
??? 250-PIPELINING
??? 250-CHUNKING
??? 250 HELP
MAIL FROM:<someone@some.domain>
??? 250
RCPT TO:<CALLER@test.ex>
??? 250
BDAT 88 LAST
>>> To: Susan@random.com
stoptls
??? 421 Lost incoming connection
???*
****
millisleep 500
killdaemon
